[901,1802],[820,1640],[739,1478],[658,1316],[577,1154],[496,992],[415,830],[334,668],[253,506],[172,344],[91,182],[10,20],[929,1858],[848,1696],[767,1534],[686,1372],[605,1210],[524,1048],[443,886],[362,724],[281,562],[200,400],[119,238],[38,76],[957,1914],[876,1752],[795,1590],[714,1428],[633,1266],[552,1104],[471,942],[390,780],[309,618],[228,456],[147,294],[66,132],[985,1970],[904,1808],[823,1646],[742,1484],[661,1322],[580,1160],[499,998],[418,836],[337,674],[256,512],[175,350],[94,188],[13,26],[932,1864],[851,1702],[770,1540],[689,1378],[608,1216],[527,1054],[446,892],[365,730],[284,568],[203,406],[122,244],[41,82],[960,1920],[879,1758],[798,1596],[717,1434],[636,1272],[555,1110],[474,948],[393,786],[312,624],[231,462],[150,300],[69,138],[988,1976],[907,1814],[826,1652],[745,1490],[664,1328],[583,1166],[502,1004],[421,842],[340,680],[259,518],[178,356],[97,194],[16,32],[935,1870],[854,1708],[773,1546],[692,1384],[611,1222],[530,1060],[449,898],[368,736],[287,574],[206,412],[125,250],[44,88],[963,1926],[882,1764],[801,1602],[720,1440],[639,1278],[558,1116],[477,954],[396,792],[315,630],[234,468],[153,306],[72,144],[991,1982],[910,1820],[829,1658],[748,1496],[667,1334],[586,1172],[505,1010],[424,848],[343,686],[262,524],[181,362],[100,200],[19,38],[938,1876],[857,1714],[776,1552],[695,1390],[614,1228],[533,1066],[452,904],[371,742],[290,580],[209,418],[128,256],[47,94],[966,1932],[885,1770],[804,1608],[723,1446],[642,1284],[561,1122],[480,960],[399,798],[318,636],[237,474],[156,312],[75,150],[994,1988],[913,1826],[832,1664],[751,1502],[670,1340],[589,1178],[508,1016],[427,854],[346,692],[265,530],[184,368],[103,206],[22,44],[941,1882],[860,1720],[779,1558],[698,1396],[617,1234],[536,1072],[455,910],[374,748],[293,586],[212,424],[131,262],[50,100],[969,1938],[888,1776],[807,1614],[726,1452],[645,1290],[564,1128],[483,966],[402,804],[321,642],[240,480],[159,318],[78,156],[997,1994],[916,1832],[835,1670],[754,1508],[673,1346],[592,1184],[511,1022],[430,860],[349,698],[268,536],[187,374],[106,212],[25,50],[944,1888],[863,1726],[782,1564],[701,1402],[620,1240],[539,1078],[458,916],[377,754],[296,592],[215,430],[134,268],[53,106],[972,1944],[891,1782],[810,1620],[729,1458],[648,1296],[567,1134],[486,972],[405,810],[324,648],[243,486],[162,324],[81,162]]},"output":2997}],"solution":"class Solution:\n    def minCostConnectPoints(self, points: List[List[int]]) -> int:\n        n = len(points)\n        INF = float('inf')\n        best = [INF] * n      # cheapest known edge from the tree to each point\n        in_tree = [False] * n\n        best[0] = 0\n        total = 0\n        for _ in range(n):\n            u = -1\n            for v in range(n):\n                if not in_tree[v] and (u == -1 or best[v] < best[u]):\n                    u = v\n            in_tree[u] = True\n            total += best[u]\n            ux, uy = points[u]\n            for v in range(n):\n                if not in_tree[v]:\n                    d = abs(ux - points[v][0]) + abs(uy - points[v][1])\n                    if d < best[v]:\n                        best[v] = d\n        return total\n","approach":"**This is a minimum spanning tree on the complete graph of points.** Any valid wiring is a spanning tree and we want the cheapest one.\n\nBecause the graph is complete (n^2 edges), the array-based **Prim's algorithm** is the natural fit: maintain `best[v]`, the cheapest edge connecting the current tree to `v`. Each of the `n` rounds scans for the unvisited point with the smallest `best`, adds it to the tree, and relaxes `best` for every remaining point using the new vertex. Correctness follows from the cut property: the lightest edge crossing the cut (tree, not-tree) always belongs to some MST.\n\n**Kruskal** is the alternative: generate all n(n-1)/2 edges, sort them, and union-find; it costs O(n^2 log n) time and O(n^2) memory, which is noticeably worse at n = 1000. A heap-based Prim also works but has the same log factor.\n\n**Common mistakes:** using Euclidean instead of Manhattan distance, forgetting the single-point case (answer 0), and pushing every edge into a heap and running out of memory.\n\n**Interview follow-ups:** Explain the cut property proof. When would you prefer Kruskal? (Sparse graphs with an explicit edge list.) How would you return the edges of the tree, not just the cost? (Record `parent[v]` whenever `best[v]` improves.)","complexity":{"time":"O(n^2)","space":"O(n)"},"similar":["network-delay-time","accounts-merge","connecting-cities-with-minimum-cost"],"number":115,"starter":"class Solution:\n    def minCostConnectPoints(self, points: List[List[int]]) -> int:\n        pass\n"}